BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paprika (2006)
DTSTART:20260418T013000Z
DTEND:20260418T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T013000Z
UID:SBWLRyk0p8
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nDr. Atsuko Chiba is a genius scie
 ntist by day\, and a kick-ass dream warrior named PAPRIKA by night. In thi
 s psychedelic sci-fi adventure\, it will take the skills of both women to 
 save the world...\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/ani-marathon
 /paprika\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Perfect Blue (1997)
DTSTART:20260418T041500Z
DTEND:20260418T055500Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T041500Z
UID:6qNGs9sjPP
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nRising pop star Mima has quit sin
 ging to pursue a career as an actress and model\, but her fans aren’t re
 ady to see her go… Encouraged by her managers\, Mima takes on a recurrin
 g role on a popular TV show\, when suddenly her handlers and collaborators
  begin turning up murdered.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/an
 i-marathon/perfect-blue\n\nEstimated start: 21:30
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Metropolis (2002)
DTSTART:20260418T193000Z
DTEND:20260418T214000Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T193000Z
UID:9JLOqoZkAf
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nBrace yourself for a totally new
  experience in cutting-edge animation. Based on the classic comic created 
 by Osamu Tezuka (Astro Boy)\, written by Japanese anime legend Katsuhiro O
 tomo (Akira) and directed by Rintaro (Galaxy Express 999)\, Metropolis is 
 a spectacular film featuring stunning imagery and unforgettable characters
 . In it\, a detective and his sidekick discover a duke's plot to control 
 the world via a humanlike robot.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-even
 ts/ani-marathon/osamu-tezukas-metropolis\n\nEstimated start: 12:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STEFF: Birds & Us
DTSTART:20260418T200000Z
DTEND:20260418T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T200000Z
UID:Iyg3TTvxvY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nPresented by GreenShower Collect
 ive Celebrate the historic launch of the 1st Seattle Taiwanese Eco Film F
 estival (STEFF)\, hosted by GreenShower. For the first time\, we are bring
 ing a curated selection of award-winning Taiwanese environmental cinema to
  the United States. This double-feature event explores our delicate bond w
 ith nature: from the investigative journey of Birds and Us to the poignant
  cultural struggle on Orchid Island in Island of People (Pongso no Tao). T
 hese films unveil the hidden environmental and social challenges facing Ta
 iwan’s ecosystems and Indigenous traditions. Join us for this landmark c
 ultural exchange\, featuring an exclusive live remote Q&A session.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/1st-seattle-taiwanese-eco-film-festiva
 l-birds-and-us\n\nEstimated start: 13:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
